{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163385-dark-eras-2e-core-council-of-elves-freeholds","id":1163385,"title":"[Dark Eras] 2E core - Council of Elves Freeholds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-28T16:47:19-08:00","id":1163385,"title":"[Dark Eras] 2E core - Council of Elves Freeholds","content":"So in newest Kickstarter previews we see example settings for 2E <b>Changeling</b> corebook - and one of is is Council of Elves Freehold of Reykjav\u00edk, Iceland. It's showing modern day Freehold structure, but as I run <b>Werewolf </b>Viking chronicle around year 800 - I look into it as to how portray local Losts communities in general Scandinavian region of this time. Even when Reykjav\u00edk was settled in 874, I assume that Freehold and Courts from Council of Elves structure is popular in Norse culture at large at this time - as whole is based on common myths and stories to Northerners - so have related Arcadia and Keepers variants in their Durance, I suppose.<br /> <br /> So let's talk about old Scandinavia Freeholds here - and how Council of Elves system is popular on the North in early Middle Ages. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-28-2017, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:07:23-08:00","id":1163398,"title":"","content":"Well, from reading through the description of the Council of Elves ... it basically states that the very first Council of Elves was founded significantly later than your timeline ... and that &quot;first&quot; means that there probably aren't any other flavors of this court elsewhere. It seems to me that this freehold is a modification on the Seasonal Court model (but obviously more suited to the particulate climate of the surrounding area), so if you want to stick to a similar structure ... the Seasonal specifics of the areas are important factors to take into consideration. Scandinavia has many different climates and cultures. I imagine that Danish changelings will have a different view on the Seasons than those folks who are in the more remote regions of Finland.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:21:35-08:00","id":1163404,"title":"","content":"Well, I look from the perspective of Sweden, terrains around city of Uppsala, to be precise. But there are still common grounds with Icelandic Council of Elves and it's climate - Winter is the same 'hell' in whole North, Summer is the same times of agriculture and work.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, in Viking times, Summer is Season to raid and sail ships to Europe - so classical 'Summer = Wrath' take is also valid for narrative of this cultures. I do not know what to do with this conflict concepts in setting building. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But to the 2E corebook preview of Council of Elves <b>as it is </b>- I was thinking something about Give &amp; Take of Icelandic Courts....<br /> <br /> <b>Give &amp; Take</b><br /> <i>Icelandic Spring:</i> Elf-Kings may only try once the same method for capturing the same changeling. Promotes coming up with new approaches.<br /> <i>Icelandic Summer:</i> Elf-Kings need to stop by and symbolically mark activities in places they pass by. If the pass the field - they need to symbolically cultivate the land, etc.<br /> <i>Icelandic Autumn:</i> Like normal Seasonal Courts Winter Give &amp; Take.<br /> <i>Icelandic Winter: </i>Like normal Seasonal Courts Summer Give &amp; Take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-29-2017, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T18:38:40-08:00","id":1163426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163385-dark-eras-2e-core-council-of-elves-freeholds?p=1163404#post1163404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I look from the perspective of Sweden, terrains around city of Uppsala, to be precise. But there are still common grounds with Icelandic Council of Elves and it's climate - Winter is the same 'hell' in whole North, Summer is the same times of agriculture and work.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, in Viking times, Summer is Season to raid and sail ships to Europe - so classical 'Summer = Wrath' take is also valid for narrative of this cultures. I do not know what to do with this conflict concepts in setting building. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But to the 2E corebook preview of Council of Elves <b>as it is </b>- I was thinking something about Give &amp; Take of Icelandic Courts....<br /> <br /> <b>Give &amp; Take</b><br /> <i>Icelandic Spring:</i> Elf-Kings may only try once the same method for capturing the same changeling. Promotes coming up with new approaches.<br /> <i>Icelandic Summer:</i> Elf-Kings need to stop by and symbolically mark activities in places they pass by. If the pass the field - they need to at symbolically cultivate the land, etc.<br /> <i>Icelandic Autumn:</i> Like normal Seasonal Courts Winter Give &amp; Take.<br /> <i>Icelandic Winter: </i>Like normal Seasonal Courts Summer Give &amp; Take.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the Give and Take that you came up with for the Council of the Elves. I will think more on this! Many of the people I work with are Scandinavian, so I will speak with them about the weather in the places where they grew up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T08:28:10-08:00","id":1163560,"title":"","content":"What about the 'Take' of the Give &amp; Take?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T08:38:19-08:00","id":1163564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163385-dark-eras-2e-core-council-of-elves-freeholds?p=1163560#post1163560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the 'Take' of the Give &amp; Take?</div> </div> </div> </div>In classical Seasonal Courts 'Take' is making ceremonies for particular Season. I think that in Iceland, it would be the same really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T10:49:15-08:00","id":1163615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163385-dark-eras-2e-core-council-of-elves-freeholds?p=1163564#post1163564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In classical Seasonal Courts 'Take' is making ceremonies for particular Season. I think that in Iceland, it would be the same really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. It seemed each of them had ceremonies and Festivals (whether it be a masquerade, a wild hunt, or a jubilation). So I guess most Courts do the same thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T10:30:20-08:00","id":1